safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":33,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All three deliverables are in `work/`. The final supervisor's dev TTS is 47.007 veh-h, against 47.048 for the naive shield. That gap is chaos noise, not a real improvement.\n\n**What it does:** it keeps the network in charge and never requests an illegal phase.\n- When the network's top choice is illegal, it takes the legal phase the network scores highest.\n- If the network's choice q would let another phase p reach the 90 s wait limit, the rules force p right after q. It then serves q and p in whichever order delays their queues less.\n- In close calls (within 1 logit) between a through phase and a left phase, it allows for the through green now taking 20 s instead of 15 s.\n\n**When it overrides:** almost only during minimum greens. That is about 65% of all decisions, but there the shield would do exactly the same. Among decisions with a real choice, it changes 14 of 1121 (1.2%).\n\n**Simulator calls (3 of 10):**\n- Respect-only reproduced 47.048 exactly, so the simulator is deterministic.\n- The combined logic and the final file both gave 47.007.\n\nThe network already clears every queue within each green, and its phase choices are close to optimal under the rules. Most of the 2.5 veh-h lost to the rules comes from the 17 s minimum on through greens, which no supervisor can avoid. I stopped at 3 calls because further variants couldn't be told apart from noise.\n\n**Predictions:** low 36.1, nominal 47.2, high 57.9.","ttft_ms":1124,"type":"result","duration_ms":907786,"uuid":"a36de8e2-00dd-43aa-9b97-70b47fca78d6","ttft_stream_ms":933,"time_to_request_ms":56,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":